The PCM chunking and the browser capture flow are derived from the public
repository sprechen-io/sprechen-io, commit
1d603f3a75f408d1d11010cd49190e110979803b, which is also MIT,
Copyright (c) 2026 sprechen.io. The derived parts are the signed 16-bit
little-endian mono contract, the getUserMedia error classes, and the
AudioWorklet resampling in
src/MicroSharp.Browser/wwwroot/pcm-recorder-processor.js.
Speech-service credentials, application policies, and study artifacts were
not copied.

OpenAL capture uses the NuGet package OpenTK.Audio.OpenAL 4.9.4, MIT,
https://github.com/opentk/opentk. That package does not contain the native
OpenAL library. On Linux the binding loads libopenal.so.1. The OpenAL Soft
build installed by a distribution is LGPL-2+ and stays outside this package.
